{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779504105,"nonce":"j+DUEX4JhHcEEjn9rf49TWlfyh0=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDJ0DjA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/166","origin":"github"},"title":"CAMP froze twice during #160 — two different recovery paths, root cause unclear","message":"## Symptom\n\nDuring [#160](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/160) (2026-05-22 deployment), **CAMP locked up twice** with different recovery paths:\n\n**Event 1 (pre-launch, ~16:??-04:00)** — Salmon log §2.\n- All-red annunciator state immediately preceding.\n- CAMP unresponsive — won't zoom or pan; \"not responding\" pop-up appeared.\n- Recovery: **full operator-stack restart on salmon**. CAMP-only reload was not attempted / not sufficient.\n- Concurrent symptom: `udp_bridge#24` first real ERROR trip in the field.\n- Coupled with WiFi-to-boat outage (salmon §3) — confounded by the boat-side WiFi router being dead at the same time.\n\n**Event 2 (mid-mission, ~19:37-04:00)** — Salmon log §8.\n- CAMP unresponsive a second time.\n- Recovery: **solo `pkill camp`** — only CAMP restarted; rest of operator stack survived.\n- WiFi was healthy at this point (Event 1's WiFi outage was already fixed via §5 physical fix). So Event 2 isn't a WiFi-coupled failure.\n\nBrief stack degradation observed between the Event 2 kill and CAMP coming back (salmon §9).\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. **Common root cause vs. two unrelated freezes?** Event 1 happened during a network-broken state; Event 2 with healthy network. Event 1 needed a full-stack restart; Event 2 needed only a CAMP restart. Are these the same underlying bug surfacing differently, or two distinct CAMP-side bugs?\n2. **Was Event 1's CAMP freeze a knock-on of `udp_bridge#24`'s ERROR trip** (event-pump blocked by a downstream consumer stuck in error state), or a parallel symptom of the WiFi outage?\n3. **What's the trigger for Event 2** with no network involvement?\n4. **Is the \"all-red annunciator → CAMP freeze\" sequence from Event 1 reproducible?** I.e., does CAMP get into a bad state when many annunciator rows transition to ERROR simultaneously?\n\n## Diagnosis path\n\n1. **Capture CAMP logs** from both events (salmon `~/.ros/log/` or wherever CAMP writes its own log). Compare error patterns.\n2. **Reproduce Event 1's stress pattern** in a controlled setting: drop boat-side WiFi router, watch annunciator + udp_bridge + CAMP behavior.\n3. **Identify Event 2's trigger** by inspecting CAMP log around 19:37 EDT — what was the boat doing? What topic/diagnostic state preceded?\n4. **Check CAMP for known event-pump bottlenecks** (single-threaded UI loop blocked by ROS callback?).\n\n## Class-prep impact\n\nFor Summer Hydro 2026: CAMP is the primary operator display. A single freeze per deployment is workable (operators can restart) but two per deployment shows a pattern. If freezes correlate with conditions students might routinely encounter (lost link, costmap traffic, etc.), this is class-quality concern.\n\nPriority: medium-to-high (not strictly class-blocking but degrades classroom-friendliness; investigate before June 4 if possible).\n\n## Context\n\n- Originating deployment: #160 (2026-05-22)\n- Salmon log: `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_salmon_logs.md` §2 (Event 1, full-stack restart), §8 (Event 2, solo kill), §9 (brief degradation post-Event-2)\n- Dev log: `docs/logs/2026/2026-05-22_dev_logs.md` — \"CAMP locked up\" entries (lines 65–67 area)\n\nPart of #160.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}